1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,224
Welcome back to part two of building a Spider-Man game

2
00:00:04,224 --> 00:00:06,246
using only artificial intelligence.

3
00:00:06,246 --> 00:00:09,661
The web swinging already worked, but our tiny hero

4
00:00:09,661 --> 00:00:12,042
still needed real superhero moves.

5
00:00:12,042 --> 00:00:15,862
First I asked the AI for a super jump.

6
00:00:15,862 --> 00:00:19,636
It launched him into the sky and made a giant

7
00:00:19,636 --> 00:00:21,658
shockwave when he landed.

8
00:00:21,658 --> 00:00:24,039
Very subtle. Totally not dangerous.

9
00:00:24,039 --> 00:00:27,814
Next came a ground slam, because every hero needs a

10
00:00:27,814 --> 00:00:30,554
button for dramatically smashing the floor.

11
00:00:30,554 --> 00:00:34,329
Then I added a power that pulls enemies closer and

12
00:00:34,329 --> 00:00:36,710
throws a huge energy ball.

13
00:00:36,710 --> 00:00:39,765
The first test looked like black spaghetti exploded

14
00:00:39,765 --> 00:00:42,866
across the city, but somehow it worked.

15
00:00:42,866 --> 00:00:45,921
For the ultimate ability, the character charged up,

16
00:00:45,921 --> 00:00:49,021
turned bright green, and became ridiculously strong.

17
00:00:49,021 --> 00:00:52,796
Finally I improved the web movement so he could zip

18
00:00:52,796 --> 00:00:55,851
between buildings, fly forward, and land with another

19
00:00:55,851 --> 00:00:57,154
enormous blast.

20
00:00:57,154 --> 00:01:00,569
Now he is less Spider-Man and more Spider-Potato with

21
00:01:00,569 --> 00:01:01,872
unlimited power.

22
00:01:01,872 --> 00:01:05,287
Which ability should I add next? Comment your wildest

23
00:01:05,287 --> 00:01:06,500
idea!
